From b03be1db1dcccc0374a7950f20105ee9e2d261f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:57:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(power): preserve thermal limits during charge inhibition

Continue input negotiation after a successful charging pause, retain the
low-FV voltage stop hysteresis across buck and CP operation, and update
JEITA FV after temperature stops. Keep charging paused if setup fails.

Expose auto and inhibit-charge through the power supply API, serialize
policy changes with suspend and teardown, and retain CP stop ownership
when the user's initial stop needs confirmation retries.

Cover thermal limits, transport failures, session changes, policy writes
and CP stop retries with UML-only KUnit tests using virtual supplies.
---
